# {{ .input_project_name }}

AgentOps project generated by [AgentOps Stacks](https://github.com/sdonohoo-db/agentops-stacks).

## Setup

### 1. Select a template

```bash
uv run setup
```

Choose from: Empty DAB, Single Agent, or Single MCP Server. Additional agent
framework templates from [databricks/app-templates](https://github.com/databricks/app-templates)
are listed and will be selectable in a future release.

### 2. Configure workspace targets

Edit `databricks.yml` and set the `host:` URL for each target (dev, staging, prod).

### 3. Validate and deploy

```bash
databricks bundle validate -t dev
databricks bundle deploy -t dev
```

## Project Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `databricks.yml` | Bundle config — variables, targets, resource includes |
| `resources/` | DAB resource definitions (auto-discovered via `include`) |
| `scripts/` | Setup and utility scripts |
| `agent_server/` | Agent code (created when Single Agent is selected) |
| `server/` | MCP server code (created when Single MCP Server is selected) |
| `app.yaml` | Databricks App config (created by setup) |

## Local Development

After selecting a template:

```bash
# Agent app
uv sync && uv run start-server

# MCP server
uv sync && uv run custom-mcp-server
```

## Deployment Targets

| Target | Mode | Trigger |
|--------|------|---------|
| dev | development | manual |
| staging | default | merge to main |
| prod | production | merge to release |
